{
  "raw": {
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-optometry-geraldton-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - Optometry - Geraldton, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lecturer - Optometry 524254 Geraldton, WA Full Time Closing on: 30 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Make a meaningful impact on rural, remote and Aboriginal eye health through a unique clinician-educator role based in Geraldton. Develop your clinical, teaching and community engagement expertise while working alongside leading academics, healthcare professionals and community partners Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: Level B, $122,876 – $145,404 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The School of Health and Clinical Sciences at the University of Western Australia is a research-intensive academic environment where excellence in research underpins teaching, learning and community impact. The School is recognised for its evidence-based approach to education, research and health improvement. This position is based in Geraldton at the Western Australian Centre for Rural Health (WACRH), one of Australia's Commonwealth-funded University Departments of Rural Health. WACRH works to improve rural, remote and Aboriginal health through education, research, student placement programs and community engagement. Working closely with the Department of Optometry and Vision Sciences, you will contribute to the delivery of culturally safe eye care services, student education and rural workforce development, supporting improved health outcomes across regional Western Australia. About the opportunity Deliver culturally safe optometry services within an Aboriginal Community Controlled Health Organisation (ACCHO), outreach programs and school-based screening initiatives while helping improve eye health outcomes in rural and remote communities. Coordinate and supervise optometry student placements, facilitate clinical education and remote learning activities, and contribute to developing the next generation of socially accountable optometrists. Build partnerships with healthcare providers, community organisations and research collaborators to expand eye health services, interprofessional learning opportunities and community-focused research initiatives. About you Therapeutically endorsed optometrist registered with AHPRA, with a commitment to delivering high-quality, person-centred and culturally safe care. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships with students, health professionals, community organisations and other stakeholders through strong communication and collaboration skills. Highly organised and self-motivated, with the ability to work independently, manage competing priorities and adapt within a dynamic rural healthcare environment. Demonstrated leadership, problem-solving and stakeholder engagement capabilities, with a strong commitment to teamwork and continuous improvement. Desirable: postgraduate qualifications, teaching experience and/or experience working in rural, remote or Aboriginal health settings. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance, WA Working with Children Check, and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD Lecturer - Optometry (524254).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Lisa Jansen (Head of Department) at l isa.jansen@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday 30 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ef4416f1 Last Name (required) 5fb8cdd6 Email (required) 5db87a68 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 2eeb3abf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Geraldton, WA, Australia Geraldton, WA, Australia First Name (required) aff95a3b Last Name (required) 19b4fed4 Email (required) f9d89101 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/associate-director-innovation-and-uplift-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Innovation and Uplift",
      "description": "Associate Director, Innovation and Uplift - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Associate Director, Innovation and Uplift 524263 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 29 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Drive strategic change and uplift across UWA’s research training services. Influence university-wide impact through innovation, data and strategy. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. About the area The University of Western Australia (UWA) is a member of Australia's Group of Eight and ranked among the top 100 universities (top 1% in the world). The Office of the Deputy Vice - Chancellor (Research) (DVC) has responsibility for research policy development and general oversight of the University’s research activities. The Graduate Research School (GRS) leads and enables research training across the University, fostering an environment in which candidates, supervisors, and partners can thrive. Operating at the intersection of talent development, research excellence, and engagement, the GRS works across the entire training lifecycle, from attraction, admissions and scholarships through to candidature support, researcher development, engagement and partnerships, thesis examination and graduation. With a team of approximately 30 staff, the GRS combines strategic leadership with operational expertise to deliver an exceptional experience for higher degree by research (HDR) candidates, early to mid-career researchers, and supervisors. The School's focus extends beyond compliance and administration to the cultivation of research talent, the strengthening of supervisory capability, and the creation of opportunities that prepare graduates to contribute across academia, industry, government and the broader community. As research training continues to evolve in response to changing workforce needs, technological transformation and growing expectations of research impact, the GRS is actively reshaping its role. Through innovation, partnership and service excellence, the GRS is building a future-focused research training ecosystem that supports individual success while advancing the University's research, innovation and societal ambitions. About the opportunity Organisational Capability and Culture Lead the ongoing development of a high-performing, engaged and future-focused professional team through workforce planning, coaching, mentoring, succession planning and professional development. Develop leadership capability and foster a collective culture of innovation, collaboration, accountability, continuous improvement and service excellence. Innovation, Improvement and Transformation Lead strategic improvement and transformation initiatives that deliver the GRS Strategic Plan and associated priorities, projects and initiatives. Promote innovation and experimentation in service delivery, business processes, systems and researcher support to enhance efficiency, effectiveness and stakeholder experience. Identify emerging trends and opportunities and translate these into organisational and operational improvements. Operational Excellence and Service Delivery Lead the ongoing design, optimisation and stewardship of the GRS operating model to ensure services remain effective, scalable, responsive and aligned with institutional priorities. Ensure services are delivered efficiently, consistently and in a manner that supports an exceptional candidate and supervisor experience. Establish and monitor service standards, performance expectations and quality assurance mechanisms. About you A postgraduate qualification and significant leadership experience in research training, higher education or another complex service environment. Strong understanding of, and ability to interpret, the Australian higher education environment and its implications for research training and service delivery. Demonstrated success building, leading and developing high-performing teams and creating cultures characterised by innovation, accountability, collaboration and continuous improvement. Demonstrated experience leading organisational capability development, operating model enhancement and service improvement initiatives within a complex service environment. Demonstrated ability to translate strategic objectives into operational outcomes. Demonstrated ability to identify emerging opportunities, challenge conventional approaches and translate innovative ideas into practical organisational improvements. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Occasional interstate and international travel may be required. Some after-hours work may be required. Position description: PD - Associate Director Innovation & Uplift 524263.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Professor Helene de Burgh-Woodman at dean-grs@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Ms. Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 29 September 2026 This position is open to international applicants. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) f1de26ee Last Name (required) cbf9a418 Email (required) 5abbcb31 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 07ce6bda Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Executive Executive Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 0615c1f8 Last Name (required) 87519521 Email (required) 27318de0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
