    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-manager-people-and-culture-service-delivery-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, People and Culture Service Delivery",
      "description": "Senior Manager, People and Culture Service Delivery - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Manager, People and Culture Service Delivery 524312 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 11 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Lead enterprise-wide People & Culture service transformation at one of Australia's leading universities Drive meaningful improvements in employee experience, service delivery, automation and digital self-service Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months About the area: People & Culture (P&C) plays a critical role in enabling The University of Western Australia (UWA) to achieve its strategic ambitions through its people. Payroll and Advisory Services delivers essential P&C services to employees and leaders across the University through the Service Centre, Payroll, and Lifecycle Transactions and Contracts teams. Together, these teams manage employee enquiries, payroll services and employment transactions across the employee lifecycle. Our focus is on delivering accurate, timely and customer-centred services supported by effective processes, technology, knowledge management and continuous improvement. About the opportunity: Lead service transformation, continuous improvement and operational excellence across the P&C Service Centre, Payroll, and Lifecycle Transactions and Contracts teams to enhance service quality, efficiency and employee experience. Optimise end-to-end employee lifecycle processes by simplifying workflows, improving cross-functional collaboration, strengthening service governance and embedding contemporary ways of working such as Agile, Scrum and Kanban. Maximise the value of ServiceNow and related enterprise service technologies to improve case management, self-service, workflow automation, knowledge management, reporting and customer experience. About you: Significant experience leading service transformation and continuous improvement initiatives within a complex, high-volume service delivery, shared services, HR operations or customer service environment. Strong practical experience using ServiceNow (ideally HR Service Delivery) or a comparable enterprise service management platform to improve workflows, case management, digital self-service, automation and customer experience. Demonstrated expertise in process improvement methodologies, including process mapping, root-cause analysis, workflow optimisation, service design and data-driven decision making. Proven ability to use service metrics, operational data and customer insights to identify improvement opportunities and deliver measurable business outcomes. Exceptional stakeholder engagement, facilitation and influencing skills, with the ability to drive change and build commitment across multiple teams without direct authority. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Senior Manager, People and Culture Service Delivery - 524312 For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply: Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Friday, 11 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University: The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity: UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number 524312. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 50f0c481 Last Name (required) 07af1509 Email (required) 3d483a05 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert bc4f89e8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Human Resources Information Technology Human Resources Information Technology Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) b1ab6c11 Last Name (required) 5a4ee8aa Email (required) fb154d95 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
