    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/identity-and-access-management-engineer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Identity and Access Management Engineer",
      "description": "Identity and Access Management Engineer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Identity and Access Management Engineer 524255 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 8 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Shape the future of digital identity at a leading university. Own complex, high-impact cyber security challenges. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a.  plus 17% superannuation. About the area UWA IT serves as a strategic enabler of teaching, learning, research, and administrative excellence. It provides the technological infrastructure, digital tools, and support services necessary to foster innovation, collaboration, and efficiency across the institution. By ensuring the reliability, security, and accessibility of education technology, research systems, and professional services platforms, IT enhances the overall experience for students, faculty, researchers, and staff. The function also drives digital transformation, supports data-driven decision-making, and ensures compliance with regulatory and cybersecurity standards. Ultimately, IT plays a critical role in advancing the university’s mission by leveraging technology to create a connected, efficient, and future-ready academic environment. About the opportunity Manage and monitor Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) platforms including Saviynt or equivalent. Automate access lifecycle events (joiner/mover/leaver), access certification campaigns, and approval workflows. Troubleshoot and resolve complex IAM issues, including access provisioning, entitlement errors, and workflow failures. About you Relevant tertiary qualification in IT, Cybersecurity, or related field, or equivalent industry certifications (e.g., CISSP, CISM, IAM/IGA vendor certifications). Proven experience configuring and managing role modelling such as RBAC, ABAC, PBAC in an enterprise-grade Identity solution. Demonstrated proficiency in scripting languages (e.g., PowerShell, Python, JavaScript) to develop and support workflows, custom rules, and automation within Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) tools. Experience with hybrid identity models (on-prem AD and Azure AD). Demonstrated knowledge of IAM concepts, including access reviews, segregation of duties (SoD), role mining, provisioning, deprovisioning, and lifecycle management. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Identity & Access Management Engineer 524255.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Daniel De Oliveira at daniel.deoliveira@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Tuesday, 8 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a q Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 89d91e19 Last Name (required) 1e720781 Email (required) 7cb1fe19 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 33dc4011 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 0593006e Last Name (required) 2b81a799 Email (required) e70d02e7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
