    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-high-performance-compute-hpc-engineer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Senior High Performance Compute (HPC) Engineer",
      "description": "Senior High Performance Compute (HPC) Engineer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior High Performance Compute (HPC) Engineer 523291 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 9 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Drive University‑wide HPC services that enable advanced research and teaching. Serve as a trusted technical authority, shaping strategy and partnerships. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The University of Western Australia – UWA has made significant investments in a new Tier2 HPC Platform to meet the research community needs enable and to align with UWA strategy and goals.  UWA is also looking to utilise technology advancements to expand its services and create new and innovative teaching and research models. The goal of High-Performance Computing team is to design and delivery operational services to the UWA research community. About the opportunity Provide insight and guidance suitable to University users on suitable pathways to achieve HPC outcomes for teaching and research activities. Provide significant input into the development of a service offering to provide HPC services available to all UWA users using a blended model of University owned, externally hosted and cloud-based platforms. Lead the maintenance, monitoring and continuous improvement of High‑Performance Computing systems, ensuring service reliability and alignment with agreed service levels. About you Relevant tertiary qualification with extensive relevant experience, or equivalent combination of experience and education. Substantial relevant computing experience in compiling and troubleshooting applications, dependencies and libraries in a mixed platform HPC environment and familiarity with compiler toolsets such as Autotools and CMake. Demonstrated experience in a range of programming and scripting languages, preferably including C++, Python, Fortran and Bash. Demonstrated experience with implementing, repairing and maintaining HPC or Linux solutions. Highly developed analytical and problem-solving skills to help maximise the benefit of the university investments. Note : Employment checks will include information on gender-based violence, sexual harassment, and related misconduct to meet legal obligations. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Senior High Performance Compute Engineer 523291.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Chris Bording at chris.bording@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 9 September 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 85d3f29e Last Name (required) 3a2b6888 Email (required) 36427ca7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 8e804c25 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 141d5672 Last Name (required) f