    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/research-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Research Officer",
      "description": "Research Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Research Officer 524173 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 3 Sep 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Lead innovative wet-lab experiments from design to discovery. Pivotal role bridging molecular biology & artificial intelligence. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: $86,540 – $95,920 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Australian Centre for RNA Therapeutics in Cancer (ACRTC) is a nationally significant RNA innovation hub based in Western Australia, dedicated to translating cutting-edge RNA science into real treatments for aggressive cancers. The Centre brings together RNA technologists, oncologists, computational biologists, AI/ML engineers, patient advocates, and industry partners to design, synthesise, test, and optimise RNA-based medicines, with a focus on hard-to-treat cancers including sarcoma, glioblastoma, hepatocellular carcinoma, triple-negative breast cancer, lung cancer, and multiple myeloma. This position sits within Capability 1: Computation, AI & RNA Multi-omics of the ROBUST program. Capability 1 will use a globally unique RNA dataset and state-of-the-art high-performance computing resources to develop one of the most data-rich RNA design platforms in the world. About the opportunity A hands-on role at the centre of landmark RNA experiments, with access to state-of-the-art research infrastructure at UWA. Training in cutting-edge nanopore direct RNA sequencing, one of the most versatile and rapidly evolving sequencing technologies. Exposure to the full drug development pipeline, from library design through to computational modelling and pre-clinical testing. About you Bachelor’s degree or relevant tertiary education in molecular biology, biochemistry, biotechnology, or a related discipline. Demonstrated hands-on experience with molecular cloning techniques (restriction cloning, Gibson assembly, Golden Gate, or similar). Demonstrated experience with mammalian cell culture (passage, transfection, and maintenance). Experience with RNA handling, extraction, and quality control (Bioanalyzer/TapeStation, Qubit, gel electrophoresis). Strong organisational skills with attention to detail in record-keeping and protocol documentation. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD [Research Officer] [524173].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Adela Foo at adela.foo@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 3 September 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) f2ac9d98 Last Name (required) 73389f1e Email (required) ec2407ff Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Solution Architect Crawley, WA Information Technology Partner with technical and business stakeholders to design, modernise and evolve the platforms that underpin UWA's operations. Senior Cybersecurity Architecture Specialist Crawley, WA Information Technology Join a high-performing team shaping UWA's cyber security future through secure-by-design and DevSecOps excellence. School Operations Officer (Music) Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services The UWA Conservatorium of Music is a dynamic and diverse hub for teaching, performance, research and community engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 36cc20b8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research support Research support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) a122d21d Last Name (required) c96ff154 Email (required) a8eb71df Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
